A wide glyph on a one-column screen has no second cell

putglyph() marks the far half of a double-width glyph by writing through
getcell() for each column after the first, and getcell() answers NULL
past the screen's edge. On a screen one column wide that is every wide
glyph -- an emoji, a CJK character -- and the write through NULL
crashed. Found by fuzzing BeerSSH's emulator under ASan; a terminal pane
can be squeezed to one column.

Skip a far cell that does not exist, and end the damage rectangle where
the screen does.

--- a/src/screen.c
+++ b/src/screen.c
@@ -190,14 +190,25 @@
   if(i < VTERM_MAX_CHARS_PER_CELL)
     cell->chars[i] = 0;
 
-  for(int col = 1; col < info->width; col++)
-    getcell(screen, pos.row, pos.col + col)->chars[0] = (uint32_t)-1;
+  /* A double-width glyph on a screen one column wide has no second
+   * cell to mark: getcell() answers NULL there, and writing through it
+   * crashed. The glyph keeps its one cell, and the damage stays inside
+   * the screen. */
+  int end_col = pos.col + info->width;
+  for(int col = 1; col < info->width; col++) {
+    ScreenCell *far = getcell(screen, pos.row, pos.col + col);
+    if(!far) {
+      end_col = pos.col + col;
+      break;
+    }
+    far->chars[0] = (uint32_t)-1;
+  }
 
   VTermRect rect = {
     .start_row = pos.row,
     .end_row   = pos.row+1,
     .start_col = pos.col,
-    .end_col   = pos.col+info->width,
+    .end_col   = end_col,
   };
 
   cell->pen.protected_cell = info->protected_cell;
